----------------------------------------------------------------------------

MIT applies to the work in this repository that is ours: the tokens, the
components, the wordmark assets and generator, `machines.json`, and the prose.
It is the content side of `198x/decisions/how-198x-licenses-its-own-work.md`,
which grants MIT for authored content and GPL-2.0-or-later for code. This is a
presentation kit for the family's own sites, not a shipped tool, and nothing in
it derives from a GPL source.

Two things the grant above does not reach.

THIRD-PARTY FONTS

`fonts/` contains no work of ours. Nebula Sans, Literata and JetBrains Mono are
redistributed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, each with its licence text
beside it:

    fonts/OFL-NebulaSans.txt
    fonts/OFL-Literata.txt
    fonts/OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt

Those files, and the `.woff2` subsets built from them, remain under the OFL and
are not licensed by this file. The OFL travels with the fonts: if you
redistribute them, carry the licence text too. See `fonts/README.md` for
provenance and subsetting.

TRADE MARKS

MIT grants copyright permissions, not trade mark permissions, and this file
grants none. The 198x name and the plate wordmark identify the projects they
belong to. Use them to refer to 198x, to link to it, or to build a site that is
part of the family; do not use them to badge something unaffiliated as 198x, or
in a way that suggests endorsement. The mark is what tells a reader which
project they are looking at, and that only works while it means one thing.
